    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Suspended chord",
      "body": "A **suspended chord** leaves out the 3rd and uses a 2nd or a 4th instead. With no 3rd it is neither major nor minor: it sounds open, as if it is waiting.\n\n**Why it matters:** Suspended chords add colour without the happy or sad label. They are all over pop and worship music, and guitarists love them.",
